version: "2.0"
name: gnomon-kernel-local
description: >-
  Local model sessions: the kernel side of running a local runner (the bundled
  or pinned runner, its endpoint and routing), brokering its tool calls through
  the supervisor, and the config request that changes the local model setup.
context:
  - >-
    bundled-runner.ts, runner-pin.ts, endpoint.ts, probe.ts and routing.ts start
    and reach the runner; tool-broker.ts brokers its tool calls;
    config-request.ts serves the config change.
  - >-
    The flows $local-brokered-call and $local-config-flow, which cross into the
    supervisor and the CLI, stay in packages/gnomon/.purpose.
  - >-
    Split out of packages/gnomon/.purpose (2026-10-27); path: values stay
    relative to packages/gnomon, the package root.
components:
  local-runner:
    description: >-
      #local-runner (spec §13, §3.3, §6.1 step 2; M1.8 slice 1). Loops step 8:
      LocalLane.openLoop(ref, req) (and supervisor.openLoop) is the ONE
      unattended open: a trusted loop run's judge/summarize step, only with a
      registry run reference; origin 'loop', surface none, maxSteps 1, no
      kernel names in the env, permit scope.loop, model text hash-only in
      turn.event, ask() returns the reply; no capable endpoint throws
      LoopModelUnavailable (no card, never Claude); isLoopSession(hsid) for
      step 12's loop.request pre-gate (see #loop-runner). Kernel side:
      local-session.ts maps a SUCCESSFUL compaction_end (summaryHash + both
      token counts, no error) onto the typed session.compacted{hsid, turn,
      reason, summaryHash, tokensBefore, tokensAfter} row (compactedPayloadOf;
      T-2026-10-18-016, P8-D93) after the raw turn.event line, which stays;
      src/kernel/local/endpoint.ts (loopback/LAN rule on the normalised host;
      hostnames, Anthropic hosts, link-local/metadata, public, userinfo,
      forbidden web-endpoint port refused — G-SUB-06 BILLING_REFUSED via
      config.ts), config.ts (compat names = gnomon-local allowlist, no cloud;
      assertNotClaude: law 7 never runs claude under a backend:local permit),
      probe.ts (/slots n_ctx, else /props, else Ollama /api/show num_ctx, else
      the loaded context in /api/ps; tools only on a live tool call),
      routing.ts (local|claude|any; capable = probe ok + tools (or text-tool
      opt-in) + n_ctx >= floor 8192), src/adapters/local/runner.ts (pi rpc
      JSONL driver, tolerant parse, LocalUsageMeter no double count),
      src/kernel/supervisor/local-session.ts (LocalLane: incapable local =>
      fallback card via the broker + model.fallback.requested +
      MODEL_UNAVAILABLE{cardId}, no spawn; fallback-cloud decision opens
      Claude, S7; any => session.routed; capable => local session.spawn
      permit recorded with model + repo (P8-D92 meter, never capped) ->
      session profile -> intend/track kind local-runner; stdout turn.event
      first, model.capabilities/model.repair, usage against the spawn
      permit). Round 2: tools confined to realpath roots (no .git, no symlink final component), probe bodies capped 1 MiB, configured model id preferred, assertNotClaude on realpaths + @anthropic-ai/claude-code, explicit backend pins the route, launchPlan TEST-RIG seam (test/local-lane-spawn.test.ts). Slice 2: config.ts loadLocalConfig reads the ROOT-SIGNED
      <home>/local.signed.json (schema gnomon-root-local:v1; unsigned, tampered,
      unparseable, invalid or older than the sidecar/chain high-water mark =>
      NO local config, logged config.unsigned / config.loaded{file,
      fallback:'none'}; a signed public endpoint is applied and refuses every
      open BILLING_REFUSED), wired by the daemon; round 2 (Aegis H1): the
      runner pin is MANDATORY (node + nodeSha256, package dir + treeSha256,
      entry) — runner-pin.ts copies the tree into <home>/runners/<treeSha256>/,
      hashes the COPY, verifies node and execs <realpath node> <realpath
      copied entry> (PERMIT_REQUIRED runner-pin-mismatch{part}); residual:
      node is not copied (Homebrew node loads ../lib) — round 3: EVERY session profile (Claude and local) denies writes to node, its install prefix and the pinned source dir (policy.ts localRunnerDenies, fed from the loaded local config), and node is re-hashed synchronously right before spawn; a concurrent staging rename (EEXIST/ENOTEMPTY) is success iff the dest verifies; turn.event rows for compaction lines keep summaryHash/summaryBytes even over the line cap; a signed config with maxTokens >= 0.85 x contextTarget is invalid; round 2 (M3): roots resolved ONCE by native realpath (fail closed) and only the resolved paths reach the policy, child config, darwin extras, repo id and spawn cwd; re-checked right before spawn; per-task endpoint choice = first endpoint in
      signed order capable for the floor; probeAll at daemon start records
      model.probe/model.capabilities; roots inside the Gnomon home refused;
      the child gets contextTarget min(~8k, n_ctx); session.send{steer} with a
      turn in flight writes the steer line under that turn's permit
      (session.inject + turn.steer, no new permit), idle it is a plain send; round 2: the steer needs the in-flight turn permit live (else PERMIT_REQUIRED); the child refuses a steer that reaches it idle and the kernel logs turn.steer{phase:refused, by:child};
      Claude sessions refuse steer BAD_REQUEST. T-2026-10-26-003: runner.ts
      parses message_end.textBytes (the reply's size, never its text) and
      agent_end input/output beside the total; local-session.ts turn.result
      keeps usage.tokens as the meter's remainder (charged once) and adds
      runUsage{tokens,input,output} (the run's whole agent_end usage) and
      replyBytes (the last assistant text's size, 0 = no answer) beside
      stopReason, so the GUI can say how the run ended; TD-2026-10-27-833:
      turn.result also carries maxSteps, the step cap written to that
      session's local.yaml (cfg.maxSteps ?? 16; a loop step its own cap), so
      the GUI's step-limit line names its number. Slice C1: tool_request lines, tools_set at open and the answers are #local-tool-broker's (see it). Deferred: darwin sandboxed
      e2e rig (G-LCL-01 fake half, G-LCL-06, 6-child G-LAW-01c), gnomon probe
      local CLI verb, the claude estimate on the card, attended/unattended
      local automations (law 5). #backend-adapter: the DRIVER half is src/adapters/local/ (runner.ts: localAdapter, LocalAdapter = core + SteerChannel + ToolBrokerChannel, LocalArgvInput, LocalUsageMeter.charge(ev); fixtures/<gnomon-local version>-turn.jsonl), called as `drv` by src/kernel/supervisor/local-session.ts; the kernel half is src/kernel/local/.
    driver-path: src/adapters/local/
    path: src/kernel/local/
    type: module
    tags: [gnomon, kernel, local, paradigm-8, m1.8]
    implements: "#backend-adapter"
    related: ["#backend-adapter", "#claude-adapter", "#gnomon-local"]
    tests:
      - test/local-runner.test.ts
      - test/local-config.test.ts
      - test/local-lane-spawn.test.ts
      - test/local-tool-broker.test.ts
    oracles: [G-SUB-06, G-LCL-02, G-LCL-03, G-ADP-02, G-LAW-01c]
  local-tool-broker:
    description: >-
      #local-tool-broker (TD-2026-10-27-833 slices S1 + C1; T-2026-10-26-003):
      the kernel half of a local session's BROKERED tools,
      src/kernel/local/tool-broker.ts, with the protocol in
      src/adapters/local/runner.ts and the wiring in
      src/kernel/supervisor/local-session.ts. S1 makes the child protocol
      two-way: child -> kernel tool_request{id tr-N, toolCallId <= 128,
      name (tool-name pattern), args (a JSON object <= 64 KiB)}, parsed into
      a typed tool-request event (closed keys; a malformed one carries
      error); kernel -> child tool_response{id, content <= 256 Ki chars,
      isError, provenance kernel | mcp:<server>} and tools_set{tools:[{name,
      description, parameters, class read|mutate|destructive}]} (the child
      applies it from its next step on); memory_set / compact / set_context
      are reserved for B2 (the child validates and parses them, applied:false).
      Every request has a deadline: TOOL_TIMEOUT_MS 30 s for read,
      CARD_TIMEOUT_MS 5 min for a carded class, the same numbers on both
      sides; the child's abort and the kernel's stop/exit cancel calls in
      flight as error results. $local-brokered-call: resolve the name in the
      OFFERED set (else unknown-tool) -> validateBrokeredArgs against the full
      schema (unknown keys always refused, types/required/enum, strings <=
      min(maxLength, 4096), arrays <= 64, depth 6, 16 KiB, no C0/C1 control or
      bidi character in keys or strings; G-LCL-15) -> class gate (read runs;
      mutate/destructive raise a `permission` card via broker.raise with
      composePermission's fenced lines, every argument shown, allow | deny,
      no Always; no decisionOf => no-approval-surface; cancel/deadline expires
      the card) -> the target (C1: the kernel's own SDK server through
      kernelMcpAnswer, kernelSdkTarget, provenance kernel; the VerbSession of
      a local session is mode ask, never plan-approved, never guarded
      worktrees) -> shapeBrokeredResult (NULs dropped, <= 64 Ki chars) -> ONE
      hash-only tool.brokered{hsid, server, tool?, class?, argsHash, decision,
      bytes, isError, cardId?} row (contracts 8.0:local-lane, closed decision
      enum, validateKindPayload) -> reply. At open LocalLane writes ONE
      tools_set (after session.sandbox, whose brokeredTools names it) with the
      C1 narrowing (offeredKernelTools: classed tools only, never the worktree
      verbs, KERNEL_TOOL_CLASSES init=mutate, push/repo-create=destructive);
      none when no kernel verbs are served (win32) and NEVER for a loop
      session (its broker offers nothing and refuses loop-session). The
      tool_request turn.event row is hash-only; requests are answered outside
      the stdout queue; at most 16 in flight per session (busy). GAPS for
      C2'/C5' (Aegis owns the class/trust grant design): no capability index
      or narrowing beyond the worktree drop; kernel verbs keep their own gate,
      so a carded verb can show the brokered card AND its own (git.push always
      does); no Always/standing grants for brokered tools; no per-server trust
      tiers (mcp:<server> provenance is plumbed but has no target yet); a card
      approved just before the child's deadline may run after the child gave
      up; control characters are refused outright (no newline in brokered
      args). Aegis C1 review (fixed): H1 one gate per call — a target that
      owns its gate (kernelSdkTarget.ownsGate: the kernel verbs) gets no broker
      card; the verb's VerbSession carries local:true plus the call's
      AbortSignal and deadline, so the queue wait, the verb card (timeoutMs =
      deadline - now, expired on abort) and the moment before the effect all
      honour them (git.verb why `cancelled`), and a local session never gets an
      Always rule, an Always choice or an auto pass; M1 the receipt time is
      stamped in the stdout handler, the kernel deadline is the child's minus
      DEADLINE_MARGIN_MS (it answers `expired` first), and the child's
      tool_cancel{id} cancels the call; M2 GitVerbs.closeSession marks the hsid
      closed (refused before any card and after the decision); M3 the run-mode
      book is read like a Claude session's (manual => the verbs refuse and no
      mutate/destructive tool is offered at open); M4 one carded call in flight
      (busy), a deny cool-down of DENY_COOLDOWN_MS per tool + args (cooldown),
      SUSPEND_AFTER_DENIES denies in SUSPEND_WINDOW_MS suspend the session
      (suspended; the row is the notice); L1 the validator refuses Cc/Cf/Co/Cn
      and default-ignorable characters and non-NFC text, checks pattern,
      minLength and type unions, and refuses a schema keyword it does not
      know; L2 runner.ts measures nesting iteratively before stringify, a line
      the parser throws on is still a hash-only row, inputHash's fallback is
      guarded; L3 the card's argsHash is the canonical inputHash and the
      tool_execution_* lines of a brokered tool are hash-only; L4 decisions
      expired and allowed-cancelled (clientApiId moved again); L5 duplicate
      in-flight ids are bad-args and toolCallId is [A-Za-z0-9_.:-]{1,128}; L6
      broker cards name the tool `kernel:<tool>` / `mcp:<server>/<tool>`; L7
      the broker exists before stdout is read (a backstop answers and logs),
      and a child that stops reading its stdin (> CHILD_STDIN_HIGH_WATER
      queued) is stopped. Aegis re-check (N1-N6, fixed): a verb's in-flight
      slot is released when its queued run settles; carded calls the child
      cancels count toward suspension and carded requests are capped at
      CARDED_PER_MINUTE; the row's decision follows the verb's closed why
      (refused for the rest, approved only on success) and carries the verb's
      cardId (kernel-mcp _meta gnomon/cardId); a request received at or before
      the session's last interrupt is cancelled; tool_cancel is honoured in the
      stdout handler ahead of the queue, and once the effect starts the kernel
      sends tool_progress{id, state running} (the child waits RUN_TIMEOUT_MS
      more, the kernel deadline stops); GitVerbs.openSession clears a closed
      hsid on open/resume; schema patterns pass unsafePattern first; the init
      verb's last cancel check precedes the remnant .git removal.
    path: src/kernel/local/tool-broker.ts
    type: module
    tags: [gnomon, kernel, local, paradigm-8, broker]
    signals: []
    tests:
      - test/local-tool-broker.test.ts
      - test/local-lane-spawn.test.ts
      - test/loop-model-e2e.test.ts
      - test/git-verbs.test.ts
    oracles: [G-LCL-15]
  local-config-request:
    description: >-
      #local-config-request (TD-2026-10-22-769; spec §13.1 "Real homes";
      G-LCL-07..G-LCL-10). A REAL home's local-model config:
      src/kernel/local/config-request.ts. validateLocalConfigInput is the ONE
      input check (shared with `gnomon dev local`): model required (<= 128),
      compat a local transport, an endpoint id, validateLocalEndpoints with
      the kernel's web port forbidden (BILLING_REFUSED), LOOPBACK ONLY in 8.0
      (dev homes too; a LAN base is ENGINE not-implemented{milestone 8.1},
      "LAN endpoints land in 8.1"), a runner dir absolute with cli.js, never
      claude. LocalConfigCards.request{op:'set', endpoint, runner?} raises ONE
      `grant` card (detail.action local.config; root class, hand only, never
      standing or always) whose allow signs ONE gnomon-root-local:v1 row
      (decision-batch.ts row table local.config: closed fields, <= 4 loopback
      endpoints, a pinned runner; helper 1.9.0, refused at RAISE on an older
      helper "update the Gnomon app", broker ROW_TABLE_MIN_HELPER); a set
      edits ONE endpoint by id and keeps the others ("unchanged" on the card);
      prepare re-pins the runner and recomputes the version (above the file,
      the sidecar and the chain high-water) under beginRootDecision, else
      "the config changed while the card was open: ask again"; the effect
      writes local.signed.json through the ONE writer (config.ts
      writeLocalConfigDoc: temp 0600, fsync, rename, never through a
      symlink) and calls the daemon's hot reload. {op:'remove'} is
      notify-and-proceed (no card): the file is deleted and the reload logs
      config.loaded{fallback:'none', why:'removed'}. request.local.probe
      {model, base?, compat?} is the read-only loopback check before a card
      (Mika C1: no card, no row, human only, one in flight, one per 2 s).
      Both are dispatcher-only (never rows; clientApiId unmoved);
      status.local (extraStatus) carries the endpoints, the runner (bundled
      or override, version, tree, node version and sha), signer, version and
      signedAt, the last probe and the last fallback, the platform
      (unsupported 'platform' on win32) and offered. bundled-runner.ts: the
      gnomon-local cli.js ships inside the kernel's dist/gnomon-local
      (tsup.config.ts bundle-gnomon-local; npm tarball and the app's
      Resources/kernel/dist), its tree hash compiled in and verified at load;
      a typed absolute runner dir overrides it. CLI raw form `gnomon local
      set|status|remove` (src/cli/local-cli.ts); the guided form is Settings
      → Local model (#gui, a separate design track).
      Aegis review (merge after fixes): the helper line shows the runner dir
      and node path in full (<= 256 chars each; never compacted; an
      OVERRIDE runner marked through the row's runnerSource); status.local
      in full to the human only (dispatch.ts localStatusFor); a remove writes
      a tombstone sidecar under beginRootDecision before the unlink, logs
      config.loaded{removed:true, version}, and no file at or below it
      applies again (loadLocalConfig chainRemoved / tombstone floor);
      nextLocalVersion counts the file only when its signature verifies; the
      sidecar goes through writeHomeFileAtomic; the probe answers for the
      configured model (listed) with one error word; no base path in 8.0,
      localhost stored as 127.0.0.1; the kernel's web and mod egress ports
      are forbidden; validateLocalEndpoints refuses non-loopback (lan-8.1);
      a bundled runner must match the compiled pin and a release build fails
      without it; an override runner must identify as gnomon-local; an
      unknown helper version on a hardware root counts as too old.
      Follow-ups: a request.local.probe of a CONFIGURED endpoint (Check
      again; base, model and compat match) reports to the LocalLane
      (LocalProbeSink: configuredEndpoint, probeGen, beginProbe,
      recordProbe): it shows as status.local.probing{probingSince,
      probingEndpoint} while it runs and refreshes status.local.lastProbe
      and the probe cache like the automatic probe (model-missing kept as
      the why); a probe begun under an older config records nothing. The
      automatic probe (probeAll) shows as probing too. LoopRunner
      status.loops.startRefused also lists every trusted loop that would be
      refused NOW (count 0, trigger 'none'), recomputed at every status
      build and config apply; still one per loop, the first fire keeps its
      since.
    path: src/kernel/local/config-request.ts
    type: module
    tags: [gnomon, kernel, local, paradigm-8, td-2026-10-22-769]
    signals: ['!config.loaded']
    gates: ['^subscription-only']
    tests:
      - test/local-config-request.test.ts
      - test/dev-local.test.ts
      - test/decision-batch.test.ts
    oracles: [G-SUB-06, G-LCL-07, G-LCL-08, G-LCL-09, G-LCL-10]
